The bell schedule is the shape of the day: how many periods there are, when each starts and ends,
and which of them are breaks. Nothing in **Timetable** works until it exists.

**You need:** access to **Timetable → Configuration**.

## Steps

1. Open **Timetable → Configuration**. It opens on the **Bell Schedule** tab.
2. Select **Create Bell Schedule** and give it a name.
3. Add periods with **Add Period**. Each period has:
   - a **label** — pre-filled as `P1`, `P2`, … and editable to whatever you call them,
   - a **start** and **end** time,
   - a **Break** switch — turn it on for intervals and lunch. Break periods are still part of the
     day, but nothing is ever scheduled into them.
4. Watch the **Schedule Preview** underneath as you go. It draws the day back to you and flags
   problems — overlapping times, a period that ends before it starts — inline, so fix them here
   rather than after saving.
5. Mark one schedule as **Default**. That is the one used for any class that isn't explicitly on
   another.
6. Select **Save Bell Schedule**. You should see **Bell schedule saved**.

## More than one schedule

You can keep several — a normal day and a half day, or different shapes for junior and senior
sections. Exactly one is the default; the rest are selected explicitly. When you
[generate the timetable](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-generate-timetable) the preflight check tells you
how many schedules it found.

## Deleting

Deleting a schedule is immediate and confirms first. Anything currently placed against it will need
re-placing, so prefer editing an existing schedule over deleting and recreating.

## What to do next

The rest of **Timetable → Configuration** can wait until you actually generate:

- **Teacher Constraints** — when each teacher is available, and their limits (default: max 6 lessons
  a day, max 3 consecutive, minimum gap 0).
- **Subjects & Rules** and **Subject Groups** — how subjects behave, and which run as a set of
  options at the same time.
- **Classrooms** — the rooms lessons can be matched to.
- **Import Data** — bulk-load setup instead of entering it screen by screen.

Next in the chain: [Grade Curriculum](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-grade-curriculum).
